(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["pharmacology-i-exam-3-diuretics-thiazide-quiz-version-2"]={"title":"Thiazide Diuretics Quiz 2 — Pharmacology I Exam 3","category":"Pharmacology I","exam":"Exam 3","sem":"fall-2026","questions":[{"q":"Which acid-base disturbance can thiazides cause?","choices":["Metabolic alkalosis","Metabolic acidosis","Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Thiazides contract the extracellular fluid and produce a metabolic alkalosis. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 26"},{"q":"Which drug is NOT a thiazide diuretic?","choices":["Metolazone","Chlorothiazide","Indapamide","Torsemide"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Torsemide is a loop diuretic; chlorothiazide, hydrochlorothiazide, chlorthalidone, metolazone and indapamide are the thiazide group. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 20"},{"q":"Which diuretic class is preferred, in low doses, for chronic hypertension?","choices":["Loop diuretics","Thiazide diuretics","Carbonic anhydrase inhibitors","Potassium-sparing diuretics"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Low-dose thiazides are preferred for hypertension, working through short-term volume loss and a chronic fall in peripheral resistance. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"A patient on a thiazide is dizzy on standing with a falling blood pressure and dry mouth. Which adverse effect is most likely?","choices":["Hyperuricemia","Volume depletion","Hypercalcemia","Photosensitivity"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Excess salt and water loss leaves the patient volume depleted, which triggers reflex responses and orthostatic symptoms. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 26"},{"q":"Which drug is a thiazide diuretic?","choices":["Furosemide","Hydrochlorothiazide","Amiloride","Acetazolamide"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Hydrochlorothiazide is a thiazide diuretic, along with chlorothiazide, chlorthalidone, metolazone and indapamide. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 20"},{"q":"Which diuretic keeps its effect at a low creatinine clearance?","choices":["Hydrochlorothiazide","Metolazone","Chlorothiazide","Amiloride"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Metolazone is effective at lower creatinine clearance rates, unlike the other thiazides. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 28"},{"q":"Which short-term mechanism lowers blood pressure with thiazides?","choices":["Direct vasodilation of arterioles","Increased renin release","Less blood volume and cardiac output","Blocked beta receptors"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. In the short term thiazides lower blood pressure by decreasing blood volume and cardiac output. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"Which of these is an indication for a thiazide diuretic?","choices":["Acute pulmonary edema","Hypokalemia","Gout","Hypertension"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Hypertension is the leading indication for thiazides, which lower blood pressure by short-term volume loss and a chronic fall in peripheral resistance. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 24"},{"q":"Which electrolyte abnormality can thiazides cause that loop diuretics do not?","choices":["Hypokalemia","Hypomagnesemia","Hypercalcemia","Hyperkalemia"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Because thiazides decrease renal calcium excretion, serum calcium can rise, so hypercalcemia is a listed adverse effect. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Which pair of minerals do thiazides cause to be lost in the urine?","choices":["Potassium and calcium","Magnesium and calcium","Potassium and magnesium","Sodium and calcium"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Thiazides increase potassium and magnesium excretion, which is why hypokalemia is a listed adverse effect. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 22"},{"q":"Which drug does a thiazide put at higher risk of toxicity through its effect on potassium?","choices":["Digoxin","Warfarin","Levothyroxine","Metformin"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Thiazides lower potassium, which increases digoxin (digitalis) toxicity. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 29"},{"q":"A patient on hydrochlorothiazide develops a sunburn after brief sun exposure. Which adverse effect is this?","choices":["Hyperuricemia","Hypercalcemia","Photosensitivity","Contraction alkalosis"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Photosensitivity and skin rashes are listed adverse effects of thiazides. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Which change in low-density lipoprotein cholesterol can thiazides cause?","choices":["An increase","A decrease","No effect at any dose","A selective rise in high-density lipoprotein"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Thiazides can increase low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, a hyperlipidemia effect. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Which group of nonspecific symptoms can occur with thiazides?","choices":["Tinnitus, vertigo and hearing loss","Gynecomastia and menstrual irregularity","Yellow vision, nausea and halos","Dizziness, headaches and weakness"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Dizziness, headaches, weakness and restlessness are nonspecific adverse effects of thiazides. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 27"},{"q":"Which preexisting condition makes a thiazide a poor choice because it can flare?","choices":["Gout","Hypertension","Calcium oxalate kidney stones","Cirrhosis with edema"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Thiazides cause hyperuricemia, which can precipitate gout, so a history of gout argues against them. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 26"}]};
